/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 653 Tm (patterns in data.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 638 Tm (A matrix is easiest to understand in the coordinate system of its eigenvectors.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 623 Tm (In principal component analysis, the eigenvectors of a covariance matrix point) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 608 Tm (along the directions where the data varies most, and the eigenvalues measure how) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 593 Tm (much variation lies along each one.) Tj
